WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.650
The curriculum runs on
the roadmap's calendar.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:07.566
The planning rule is simple: no gate is
scheduled without its training dates, and no

3
00:00:07.566 --> 00:00:12.338
wave without its training window, so a wave
that slips moves its training with it.

4
00:00:12.338 --> 00:00:15.888
Each gate carries a training
check beside its technical exit.

5
00:00:15.888 --> 00:00:18.934
At the foundation gate,
the help desk is trained on

6
00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:22.725
verification and administrators
on just-in-time activation.

7
00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:26.013
Pilot and division users are
trained before their waves.

8
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:30.499
And by the last gate, no course still
teaches an Active Directory procedure.

9
00:00:30.499 --> 00:00:34.708
The help desk goes first: no
technician is made eligible for a help

10
00:00:34.708 --> 00:00:39.150
desk role until their training and
verification check are on record.

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.956
Before each wave, champions and managers
start sixty to forty-five days out,

12
00:00:43.956 --> 00:00:49.226
the help desk is trained by thirty days,
users are assigned their modules at thirty,

13
00:00:49.226 --> 00:00:53.470
with reminders at fifteen and seven,
and then the readiness check.
